url: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  Community research on integer multiplication. The selected maintainer-reviewed
  conditional finite composition has kappa = 51110230636731/31250000000000000
  = 0.001635527380375392. Chafik Boukhalfa's PR626 allocation on Jeremy Kothe's PR622/PR623 construction composes
  with eumemic's PR543 interleaved-source bit supplier, building on cold
  kernels, entrance promotions, shared prefixes, exact owner allocation,
  frame coalescences, hyperplane-ended helpers and the cumulative community framework. Parallel
  constructions, verification tools and scoped research results are preserved.
  All-size/compiler/common-label/mutable-basis, pooled-cell hosting, normalized
  residual, precision/tape and analytic-transfer interfaces remain conditional.
  Finite checks do not constitute a complete Lean multiplication theorem.
